= Epistemic status =

[[Has type::Text]]

The present '''evidentiary standing''' of a page, section, or claim when such metadata is useful.

Canonical V2 values:

* <code>Hypothetical</code>
* <code>Emerging</code>
* <code>Supported</code>
* <code>Well-supported</code>
* <code>Established</code>
* <code>Disputed</code>

The first five describe broad regions of evidentiary maturity. <code>Disputed</code> marks credible unresolved conflict and is not simply another rung on the same ladder.

Do not use this property for:

* lifecycle (<code>Archived</code>, <code>Deprecated</code>, <code>Superseded</code>);
* review state (<code>Reviewed</code>, <code>Verified</code> without explaining what was verified);
* constitutional/foundational role (<code>Axiomatic</code>);
* numerical confidence.

See [[BITwiki:Epistemic status]] and [[BITwiki:Epistemics]].
